---
// 01 — Letter from the Founder.
---
<section id="letter" class="relative border-t border-ink/10 bg-paper-deep/40">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="md:col-span-8">
        <p
          class="reveal font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.3em] text-ink-faint uppercase"
        >
          01 &mdash; Letter from the Founder
        </p>
        <h2
          class="reveal mt-6 font-display text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight text-ink md:text-5xl"
          style="--reveal-delay: 80ms"
        >
          Dear reader,
        </h2>
        <div
          class="reveal mt-8 max-w-2xl space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.85] text-ink-soft"
          style="--reveal-delay: 160ms"
        >
          <p>
            Octopy is a software studio of one. There is no org chart in this report &mdash;
            the founder writes the code, runs the servers, answers the email, and sweeps the
            floor.
          </p>
          <p>
            For the past decade I have worked where code meets infrastructure: building web
            applications and running the servers underneath them, for government agencies and
            private clients. Along the way I started publishing the tools I kept rebuilding
            &mdash; most notably
            <a
              href="https://github.com/octopyid/laravel-impersonate"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="text-ledger underline decoration-ledger/40 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-ink"
              >laravel-impersonate</a
            >, a user-impersonation package for Laravel now carrying 300+ stars on GitHub.
          </p>
          <p>
            This year the studio&rsquo;s flagship product, Poka, moved from closed testing
            toward public release. The lab kept humming &mdash; Tako, our self-hosted
            platform, took its current shape. Everything you will find in the following pages
            was built the same way: by hand, on purpose, without an assembly line.
          </p>
          <p>
            Thank you for reading. If any of this is useful to you &mdash; the software, the
            notes, or the example &mdash; then the year was a good one.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="reveal mt-10 font-display text-2xl text-ink italic" style="--reveal-delay: 220ms">
          &mdash; Supian M.
        </p>
        <p
          class="reveal mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.25em] text-ink-faint uppercase"
          style="--reveal-delay: 260ms"
        >
          Founder, Octopy
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="md:col-span-4">
        <figure class="reveal md:sticky md:top-28" style="--reveal-delay: 200ms">
          <div class="border border-ink/15 bg-paper p-3 shadow-[0_16px_36px_-18px_rgb(22_19_16/0.35)]">
            <img
              src="/images/supian.webp"
              alt="Supian M., founder of Octopy"
              class="aspect-square w-full object-cover"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption
            class="mt-4 flex items-center justify-between font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-faint uppercase"
          >
            <span>Fig. 1 &mdash; The founder</span>
            <span>2026</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
